  runners/thermal-soak, runners/gpu-burn, runners/power-swing
    - no third-party component. All three images are built entirely from this
      project's own Apache-2.0 source (thermal_soak.cu / gpu_burn.cu /
      power_swing.cu over a shared soak_core.cuh), reaching NVML by dlopen
      against the driver's libnvidia-ml.so.1 at runtime, with no NVIDIA header
      vendored.

      Stated explicitly rather than omitted, because "gpu-burn" is the name of
      an existing project and the absence of an entry here would otherwise look
      like an oversight. This image contains NO code from wilicc/gpu-burn. That
      project's own licence is BSD-2-Clause and would have been acceptable; the
      obstacle is what it links. Its numeric core is cuBLAS, which is covered by
      the NVIDIA CUDA EULA and is a TOOLKIT library rather than a driver
      library — the NVIDIA Container Toolkit injects libcuda.so.1 and
      libnvidia-ml.so.1 from the host, and does not inject libcublas. Shipping a
      working cuBLAS-based image would therefore mean redistributing an NVIDIA
      redistributable, which the runner-image rule in CLAUDE.md forbids. The
      kernel here is an independently written SGEMM; only the METHOD (repeat a
      large GEMM, compare each result against the first, count differing
      elements) is common, and a method is not a copyrightable work.

